@*
    A REFUSED feature: something this build will not do, drawn inert, with the reason in the danger
    tone (design §4.1; docs/architecture/admin-dashboard-review.md, F-6). Danger, not warning, since the
    final branch review's item 11: the warning tone is a warned subsystem's, and one refused slot read
    amber on one screen and red on the next.

    Never drawn like NotYetPanel. A warned subsystem is somewhere the operator can stand; this is a
    control, or a whole capability, whose only outcome would be a refusal — so it reads as unavailable
    rather than as merely quiet.
*@
<div @attributes="Attributes" class="@CssClass.Of("a-refused", Attributes)">
    <span class="a-refused__reason">@ChildContent</span>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>Why it is refused, and where the thing it needs would come from.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Anything else, onto the refusal's element — a <c>data-testid</c>.</summary>
    [Parameter(CaptureUnmatchedValues = true)]
    public IReadOnlyDictionary<string, object>? Attributes { get; set; }
}
